---
// How one certificate gets issued: CSR in, DNS-01 through the CNAME, certificate out.
---

<figure class="kk-diagram">
  <div class="kk-scroll">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="flow-title flow-desc">
    <title id="flow-title">How KrakenKey issues a certificate</title>
    <desc id="flow-desc">
      Your host, pipeline or key vault creates the private key and a CSR and sends only the CSR to KrakenKey.
      KrakenKey places the ACME order with Let's Encrypt. Let's Encrypt looks up the _acme-challenge name in
      your DNS, which is a CNAME into KrakenKey's DNS zone, where KrakenKey has published the challenge answer.
      The certificate and chain go back to where the key is.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="flow-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="kk-arrowhead"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- Top row -->
    <rect class="kk-box kk-yours" x="10" y="20" width="210" height="110" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-title" x="115" y="52" text-anchor="middle">Your host, pipeline or vault</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="115" y="78" text-anchor="middle">Creates the private key and CSR</text>
    <text class="kk-note kk-strong" x="115" y="100" text-anchor="middle">The key stays here</text>

    <rect class="kk-box kk-ours" x="290" y="20" width="180" height="110" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-title" x="380" y="52" text-anchor="middle">KrakenKey</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="380" y="78" text-anchor="middle">Checks the CSR against</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="380" y="96" text-anchor="middle">your verified domains</text>

    <rect class="kk-box" x="540" y="20" width="210" height="110" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-title" x="645" y="52" text-anchor="middle">Let's Encrypt</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="645" y="78" text-anchor="middle">Validates the domain</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="645" y="96" text-anchor="middle">and signs the certificate</text>

    <!-- 1: CSR -->
    <line class="kk-line" x1="220" y1="55" x2="288" y2="55" marker-end="url(#flow-arrow)"></line>
    <text class="kk-label" x="254" y="45" text-anchor="middle">1 CSR</text>
    <!-- 2: ACME order -->
    <line class="kk-line" x1="470" y1="55" x2="538" y2="55" marker-end="url(#flow-arrow)"></line>
    <text class="kk-label" x="504" y="45" text-anchor="middle">2 order</text>
    <!-- 5: cert back -->
    <line class="kk-line" x1="538" y1="105" x2="472" y2="105" marker-end="url(#flow-arrow)"></line>
    <line class="kk-line" x1="288" y1="105" x2="222" y2="105" marker-end="url(#flow-arrow)"></line>
    <text class="kk-label" x="254" y="125" text-anchor="middle">5 cert</text>
    <text class="kk-label" x="504" y="125" text-anchor="middle">4 cert</text>

    <!-- Bottom row: DNS -->
    <rect class="kk-box kk-yours" x="10" y="210" width="330" height="100" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-title" x="175" y="240" text-anchor="middle">Your DNS (set up once)</text>
    <text class="kk-mono" x="175" y="266" text-anchor="middle">_acme-challenge.example.com</text>
    <text class="kk-mono" x="175" y="288" text-anchor="middle">CNAME example-com.acme.krakenkey.io</text>

    <rect class="kk-box kk-ours" x="420" y="210" width="330" height="100" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="kk-title" x="585" y="240" text-anchor="middle">KrakenKey DNS zone</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="585" y="266" text-anchor="middle">Holds the TXT answer for each</text>
    <text class="kk-note" x="585" y="288" text-anchor="middle">challenge, then removes it</text>

    <!-- KrakenKey publishes the answer -->
    <line class="kk-line kk-dashed" x1="410" y1="130" x2="540" y2="208" marker-end="url(#flow-arrow)"></line>
    <text class="kk-label" x="440" y="185" text-anchor="start">publishes</text>
    <!-- 3: Let's Encrypt looks up the name -->
    <path class="kk-line kk-dashed" d="M690,130 L690,170 L175,170 L175,208" fill="none" marker-end="url(#flow-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="kk-label" x="200" y="162" text-anchor="start">3 Let's Encrypt looks up the challenge</text>
    <!-- CNAME follow -->
    <line class="kk-line" x1="340" y1="275" x2="418" y2="275" marker-end="url(#flow-arrow)"></line>
    <text class="kk-label" x="379" y="265" text-anchor="middle">CNAME</text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    The only thing that leaves your side is the CSR. Because the challenge record lives in KrakenKey's zone, renewals need no DNS changes and no DNS credentials on your hosts.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
